~ assignement_given

professor: Alright, listen up, everyone. I know how much you *love* assignments, so here’s a little gift for you.  

professor: Your next assignment is due at the end of the week. Yes, that means *this* week, not "whenever you feel like it."  

professor: It’s a simple task—if you actually paid attention in class, that is. Write a well-structured analysis on today's topic, using *real* sources. And no, Wikipedia doesn't count.  

professor: Plagiarism? Oh, please, surprise me and *don’t* copy-paste half your paper from some sketchy website. I *will* check.  

professor: Late work? Love the enthusiasm, but no. If you have a *real* reason, tell me before the deadline, not after you've mysteriously "lost your file" five minutes before submission.  

professor: And please, do me a favor—proofread your work. If I see another essay that looks like it was written by a sleep-deprived raccoon, I might actually reconsider my career choices.  

professor: That’s it. Have fun, don’t disappoint me (again), and try not to make me regret giving you this assignment.  



=> END